  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The process and conservation matches are supported. Nonacceptance remains warranted, but a vacuous supplementary accuracy clause must not be confused with global theorem vacuity, and conditional error hypotheses must be distinguished from restrictions defining method quality.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target supplies chronological execution and conservative updates; D051 defines quality; the native joint application exhibits four cells and a moving nonconstant array."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The missing stability-witness meaning is resolved by additional declaration evidence. The unresolved smooth-reference interpretation and effective method-domain comparison remain material.",
      "primary_evidence": "LineFamily.stabilityRate is explicitly Classical.choose quality.stability in the supplied local definition; stabilityRate_spec states its nonnegativity and pairwise estimate. D197 stops at ContDiffWithinAt."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined and accepted=false. Established defects prevent acceptance, while the complete reverse semantic implication remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "The classification policy requires preserving unresolved implication meaning. The exact user receipt requires smooth-solution order and quantitative control near discontinuities without specifying the target's full quality predicate."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined, independently of agreement between judges. The stability concern is no longer a reason for uncertainty; reference-class and domain correspondence are.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native stabilityRate_spec resolves amplification linkage. SpatialSmoothReferenceOn still invokes an unexpanded ContDiffWithinAt regularity condition."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D020 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved: stabilityRate selects the witness from quality.stability. It is nonnegative and satisfies the advertised uniform admitted-input stability inequality; it is not necessarily minimal or canonical.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplied RefiningLineMethod definition reads Classical.choose quality.stability. The proof-free native stabilityRate_spec gives 0 ≤ stabilityRate and the factor 1 + stabilityRate * dt."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D043 unclear",
      "resolution": "Its conjunction and exact regularity argument are understood. Equivalence of its reference class with the convention's smooth solutions remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D043 requires ContDiffOn Real WithTop.top.top on the closed space-time rectangle, SpatialRectangleReferenceOn, and state membership. Printed page 103 uses smoothness without this formal index."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D197 unclear",
      "resolution": "ContDiffOn requires ContDiffWithinAt at every point of the specified set. The supplied evidence does not expose the latter predicate's outer-top case, so neither ordinary infinite differentiability nor analyticity is certified here.",
      "primary_evidence": "D197 supplies only the reduction to ContDiffWithinAt. The native supplement repeats ContDiffOn ℝ ⊤ without expanding that predicate."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D204 unclear",
      "resolution": "The declaration itself is resolved: ENat is WithTop Nat. Its meaning does not determine the calculus interpretation of an additional outer top.",
      "primary_evidence": "D204 explicitly defines ENat as WithTop Nat; D197 takes an index in WithTop ENat."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D266 unclear",
      "resolution": "Top.top projects the greatest element of the selected instance. Measure infinity and the regularity index are distinct typed uses; uncertainty belongs to the calculus consumer.",
      "primary_evidence": "D266 is the Top projection. D043 uses it at WithTop ENat, whereas D069 excludes the ENNReal top from physical cell measures."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D269 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved as a type construction: WithTop adds an outer element through Option. It does not identify that element with the embedded top already present in ENat.",
      "primary_evidence": "D269 defines WithTop α as Option α; D204 defines ENat as WithTop Nat."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D270 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolved: the added top is Option.none. Its analytic meaning remains a question about ContDiffWithinAt, not this constructor.",
      "primary_evidence": "D270 explicitly supplies top := Option.none."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Measure, norm, averaging, update and stability meanings are resolved. The smooth-reference calculus frontier remains unresolved, so C06 cannot receive an unconditional pass.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native supplement identifies Lebesgue normalization, maximum-component norms, Bochner integrals and stabilityRate_spec. It does not expand ContDiffWithinAt."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "Finite real states, signed line indices and finite cells are explicit. The target additionally restricts supplied families and realizations; equivalence with the whole interpreted source domain is not established.",
      "primary_evidence": "D053 requires comparable refining meshes and fixed interior coverage; D061 fixes ghost values; D063 requires synchronized selected time steps and exact realization identities. Q10 specifies connectivity, physical volumes and shared normal fluxes."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Reference integrability, admission and defect bounds are legitimate premises for a conditional error estimate. However, inserting pairwise Lipschitz stability into the definition of every high-resolution family is an additional quality requirement, not an explicit requirement of the receipt.",
      "primary_evidence": "D051 includes stability as a conjunct of HasControlledHighResolution. The exact receipt leaves norm, CFL and variation choices unspecified and requires order greater than one and quantitative oscillation control."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Sequential execution and conditional error propagation are present. General coverage of nonsmooth inputs is not guaranteed by the quality predicate, and no accuracy guarantee at the selected level follows from its cell-specific threshold clause.",
      "primary_evidence": "D051 restricts oscillation control to admitted arrays and automatically admits only eventual qualifying smooth projections. The target has ∃C,N, N ≤ selectedLevel → estimate."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve D020 using the direct definition and native specification. Retain the independently unresolved smooth-reference regularity meaning.",
      "primary_evidence": "Classical.choose quality.stability appears in the supplied definition, and stabilityRate_spec supplies the selected witness's property. D197 exposes no outer-top calculus branch."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Conservation signs and inequality directions are correct. Additional premises reduce applicability and cannot establish faithful-stronger status. The target does not assert unconditional effectiveness or composite second-order accuracy.",
      "primary_evidence": "D039 subtracts right-minus-left numerical flux; D033 integrates left-minus-right physical flux. Printed page 6 gives a qualified practical assessment."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target handles compatible supplied realizations, including multiple directions, but does not establish equivalence of that domain with all methods and logical grids covered by the recorded conventions. A common line scaling alone is not a demonstrated geometric counterexample: spatially varying line flux can absorb geometry.",
      "primary_evidence": "D012 permits position-dependent flux. D063 requires volume, duration and constant-state flux compatibility. Q10 does not prescribe these exact identities, and the native joint witness uses one direction."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C12 unclear",
      "resolution": "Global impossibility and identity-only execution are refuted by the joint witness. The fixed-level accuracy clause is independently vacuous when N exceeds the selected level. The family-wide eventual estimate is not vacuous for that reason, although its reference and admission coverage still require scrutiny.",
      "primary_evidence": "DIMJointPrimaryWitness.full_application, actual_geometry, active_count and initial_moves give a nontrivial application. The target's cell-specific existential threshold is chosen after the stage and cell."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N03 unclear",
      "resolution": "The amplification premise is correctly linked to the selected stability rate. The resulting recurrence is a conditional forward cell-mean error bound, separate from oscillation control. Neither small defects nor convergence follow without further assumptions.",
      "primary_evidence": "stabilityRate_spec gives the requisite pairwise estimate. D046 defines B(n+1)=amplification(n)B(n)+localDefect(n)+splittingDefect(n); the target supplies the separate defect bounds."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N05 unclear",
      "resolution": "Family accuracy has meaningful eventual quantifiers and a local defect C dt h^p with p>1. The executed-level clause adds no unconditional accuracy guarantee. Whether the family estimate covers the adopted smooth class remains unresolved.",
      "primary_evidence": "D051 places p before q and C,N before all sufficiently large levels. D053 requires mesh convergence. D043 supplies the unresolved regularity class."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "Retain unclear for complete semantic correspondence, while resolving the alleged missing stability linkage. The conditional algebraic consequences can be justified from the supplied quality and defect assumptions without deriving those assumptions from the book.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target and stabilityRate_spec support the conditional recurrence. The exact high-resolution receipt does not define HasControlledHighResolution or settle its smooth-reference domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve negatively for the complete interpreted claim: correct sequential execution does not by itself recover the required method-quality coverage near discontinuities. Admission of actual arrays is assumed, and no general nonsmooth coverage condition is supplied.",
      "primary_evidence": "D009 and D053 permit arbitrary admission predicates; D051 guards oscillation estimates by admission. Printed pages 5–6 and 103–104 emphasize discontinuous solutions, and the user explicitly adopts quantitative control near discontinuities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The translation's unknown coefficient can now be identified with the nonnegative stability witness. Its complete equivalence with the interpreted source remains unresolved because the exact smooth-reference class and additional method-domain requirements are not established as equivalent.",
      "primary_evidence": "The direct definition and native stabilityRate_spec resolve rho. D043/D197 and D051/D053/D063 retain the reference-class and effective-domain issues."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected Q10 interpretation and the applicable literal user high-resolution interpretation, the target correctly represents successive conservative coordinate execution and conditional error propagation. It does not ensure that the supplied quality package covers the nonsmooth inputs required by the adopted interpretation: oscillation control is guarded by an arbitrary admission predicate, while automatic admission concerns only eventual qualifying smooth projections. The nontrivial advection witness establishes one valid instance, not this general coverage. Additional stability and realization requirements also cannot be treated as stronger conclusions."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "Under those same separately attributed interpretations, the conditional execution, conservation and error-estimate formulas are supported once the target's actual hypotheses are supplied; D020 no longer obstructs their mathematical interpretation. However, complete source-to-target semantic correspondence still depends on the unexpanded outer-top regularity condition and the relationship between the adopted method-quality domain and the target's more specific quality and realization structures. The source and receipts do not establish that equivalence. This uncertainty concerns the audited meaning, not a claim that the displayed conditional algebra is false."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The supplied evidence does not expose ContDiffWithinAt's interpretation of the outer top in WithTop ENat. No definitive identification with ordinary smoothness or analyticity is made.",
    "Equivalence between the full recorded logical-grid/method scope and the target's compatible realization domain is not established. The one-direction joint witness establishes satisfiability, not general multidimensional representability.",
    "The printed source leaves logical rectangularity, scheduling details and quantitative high-resolution criteria unspecified. The recorded conventions resolve only their stated portions.",
    "Source, transport and artifact hashes are supplied provenance; they were not independently recomputed in this tool-free adjudication."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "insufficient-nonsmooth-admission-coverage",
      "evidence": "D051 requires variation control only when family.admitted n values holds. D053 permits an arbitrary admission predicate. Its only automatic admission requirement is eventual admission of projections of D043 references.",
      "impact": "The general quality predicate does not guarantee control on an intended class of discontinuous inputs. The separate all-admitted advection instance does not strengthen the universally quantified target."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "vacuous-fixed-level-accuracy-clause",
      "evidence": "For each fixed stage and cell, the target allows ∃C,N followed by N ≤ selectedLevel → estimate. Choosing N=selectedLevel+1 defeats the premise.",
      "impact": "This conjunct cannot independently certify accuracy at the executed level. It does not invalidate the distinct family-wide eventual estimate or make the entire theorem vacuous."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "unresolved-smooth-reference-domain",
      "evidence": "D043 uses ContDiffOn Real WithTop.top.top; D197 stops at ContDiffWithinAt. D204 and D269 establish two distinct top layers but do not supply their calculus meanings.",
      "impact": "Smooth-order and automatic-admission coverage cannot be certified against the literal adopted convention."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "additional-quality-and-realization-restrictions",
      "evidence": "D051 adds uniform pairwise maximum-norm Lipschitz stability; D053 imposes mesh comparability; D061 fixes ghosts; D063 requires compatible selected levels, durations, volumes and fluxes.",
      "impact": "These are explicit applicability restrictions. They cannot justify faithful-stronger classification, although some are reasonable premises for a separately identified conditional analysis theorem."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "resolved-stability-and-operator-semantics",
      "evidence": "The supplied definition selects quality.stability, and stabilityRate_spec gives its exact bound. Native evidence also identifies Lebesgue measures, maximum-component norms and the Bochner integral construction.",
      "impact": "The blind D020 uncertainty and associated amplification-linkage objection are resolved. Reuse provenance alone was not used as proof of task-specific correctness."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "genuine-process-linkage-and-satisfiability",
      "evidence": "D031, D039–D041, D050, D063 and D080 connect the actual recurrence to conservative line advances. The native joint witness has four measured cells, positive duration and a moving nonconstant initial array.",
      "impact": "The theorem has substantive executable mathematics and satisfiable joint premises. Physical conservation remains distinct from numerical approximation, and no unconditional effectiveness or composite convergence theorem is asserted."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The primary images support successive coordinate-direction solves on rectangular or logically rectangular grids, with high-resolution terminology accommodating discontinuities. The separately recorded Q10 and user quality conventions apply with their original authority and scope. Inspection of the supplied definitions resolves the stability witness, measure normalization, norm and execution semantics. It also confirms that the fixed-level threshold clause is vacuous in isolation and that nonsmooth admission coverage is not guaranteed. The exact smooth-reference calculus meaning and full effective-domain correspondence remain unresolved. Therefore this is a nonaccepted, undetermined adjudication, not a majority vote or a finding of unconditional mathematical falsity."
}
